WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.286
<v Jordan Ruiz>Priya, good morning. Wanted to follow up live rather than over email — we got approval for 12% off the 3-year term, and Greg confirmed the redlines on payment terms and renewal are all acceptable on our side.</v>

00:00:16.986 --> 00:00:26.414
<v Priya Nair>That works for us. I looped in Greg yesterday and he's fine with 12% given everything else lined up. Let's move forward.</v>

00:00:27.114 --> 00:00:35.686
<v Jordan Ruiz>That's great news. I'll send the final contract via DocuSign within the hour — Greg and you both as signers?</v>

00:00:36.386 --> 00:00:37.671
<v Priya Nair>Yes, that's right.</v>

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:50.800
<v Jordan Ruiz>Once that's signed, I'll get our Customer Success team looped in immediately to schedule onboarding. Given your October target, we'll want to kick that off next week if possible.</v>

00:00:51.500 --> 00:01:04.357
<v Priya Nair>Works for us. Wes Coleman will be the day-to-day technical contact on our side going forward — I'll still be involved but he'll be closer to the actual pipeline builds.</v>

00:01:05.057 --> 00:01:14.057
<v Jordan Ruiz>Perfect, I'll make sure our CSM, Riley Thompson, has Wes's contact details and gets a kickoff on the calendar this week.</v>

00:01:14.757 --> 00:01:21.186
<v Priya Nair>Sounds good. Glad this is coming together — thanks for being flexible on the terms.</v>

00:01:21.886 --> 00:01:29.600
<v Jordan Ruiz>Thank you both for the trust — looking forward to getting you live well ahead of peak season.</v>
